{"\001Then why not describe this “cycle”\002?\nIf you wish. A server is woken at hour \003four-thirty\004 by stimulin in the airflow, then yellow-up in our dormroom. After a minute in the hygiener and steamer, we put on fresh uniforms before filing into the restaurant.","Cloud Atlas","David Mitchell",true},
{"“What time is it? Do you have time here?”\n“Of course we do.” She pulled up her sleeve, revealing a yellow Timex wristwatch. “It is \003four thirty in the morning\004.”\n“That’s a nice watch.”\n“My father gave it to me,” she said happily.","The Catacombs","Jeremy Bates",true},
{"At the end of a relationship, it is the one who is not in love who makes the tender speeches. I was overwhelmed by a sense of betrayal, betrayal because a union in which I had invested so much had been declared bankrupt without my feeling it to be so. Chloe had not given it a chance, I argued with myself, knowing the hopelessness of these inner courts announcing hollow verdicts at \003four thirty\004 in the morning.","Essays in Love","Alain de Botton",true},
