["04:49"]={
{"When Costain left the bridge the brass chromometer in the wheelhouse said \003eleven minutes to five\004. Harkness looked at it and realised vaguely that the gap was still too big.","Gale Force","Elleston Trevor",true},
},
["04:50"]={
{"Even the hands of his watch and the hands of all the thirteen clocks were frozen. They had all frozen at the same time, on a snowy night, seven years before, and after that it was always \003ten minutes to five\004 in the castle.","The 13 Clocks","James Thurber",true},
},
["04:51"]={
{"\0034:51 A.M.\004\n“You know, I hate to spoil all the fun you’re having.” Vance tried to look at Moreau, but he could barely see through the swelling of his puffy eyelids. “But I’ve got some unsettling news. You and the rest of Ramirez’s hoods are about to be in a deep situation here. The minute you try to send that bomb up, you can tip your hat and kiss your ass good-bye. Better enjoy this while you can.”","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover",false},
{"Earlier? It’s \003nine minutes to five a.m.\004 — who would be up this early?\n“Oh, we’re all early risers.”","Gifts of the Magi","Jean Johnson",true},
},
["04:52"]={
{"Anna left the apartment at \0034:52 A.M.\004, dressed in jeans, a blue T-shirt, a linen jacket, and a baseball cap. She wasn’t sure what to expect as she stepped out onto the sidewalk that cool, dark morning.","False Impression","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"If it matters, it’s \003eight minutes to five\004. Don’t get any persecuted ideas that I enjoy being out of bed at this time of night. It makes it legally easier if you invite us in.","Holding the Zero","Gerald Seymour",true},
},
["04:53"]={
{"It was so quiet in the post office that Trinidad could hear the soft tick of the clock’s second hand every time it moved. It was now \003seven minutes before five\004.","The Silence of Bonaventure Arrow","Rita Leganski",true},
},
["04:54"]={
{"When the last lid had been placed back on he checked the clock on the wall: \003six minutes to five\004. Just enough time to glance in the other box and see if he could expect the same again.","A Matter of Honor","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"\003Six minutes to five\004. Six minutes to go. Suddenly I felt quite clearheaded. There was an unexpected light in the cell; the boundaries were drawn, the roles well defined. The time of doubt and questioning and uncertainty was over.","Dawn: A Novel","Elie Wiesel",true},
},
["04:55"]={
{"There were two messages. The first, sent at \0034:55 a.m.\004, was from the campus garage.\n“We have your vehicle,” the mechanic’s voice informed him. “Unfortunately, we had some trouble getting it out of the ditch, and it has sustained a small amount of additional damage.”","The Enclave","Karen Hancock",true},
{"\0034:55\004 — Mank holding phone. Turns to Caddell — “Who is this?”\nCaddell: “Jim.” (shrugs) “I think he’s our man in Cincinnati.”","Fear and Loathing: On the Campaign Trail ’72","Hunter S. Thompson",true},
},
["04:56"]={
{"Trying to identify the key facts, Ethan was suddenly aware he was looking at the wall clock; it was 7:35.\n“Wait a minute. When did you hear about this?”\nThere was a tiny moment of hesitation. “The first news came in \003just before five\004.”","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley",true},
{"“That’s it. At \003four minutes to five\004 by yours. Seven to, by mine.”\nIt was the cuirassier who remained by the side of General D’Hubert, keeping his one eye fixed immovably on the white face of the watch he held in the palm of his hand. He opened his mouth wide, waiting for the beat of the last second, long before he snapped out the word:\n“Avancez!”","The Point of Honor","Joseph Conrad",true},
},
["04:57"]={
{"One hundred and thirty-one seconds were lost at Elkhart in changing locomotives, and it was \003three minutes to five\004 when big 599, with Dave Luce in the cab, turned her nose toward the dawning day and started for Toledo, 133 miles away.","Careers of Danger and Daring","Cleveland Moffett",true},
{"It was not until they had swept through the village, over the bridge, and were out on the broad highway toward Chester that Ruth began to realize what a wild goose chase she had undertaken. Just where did she expect to find them, anyway? It was now \003three minutes to five\004 by the little clock in the car and it was a full fifteen minutes’ drive to Chester.","The Search","Grace Livingston Hill",true},
{"The second said the same thing a \003few minutes before five\004, and mentioned eternity… I’m sure I’ll meet you in the other world. Four minutes later she left a last, fleeting message: My love. Fernando. It’s Suzana. Then, it seemed, she had shot herself.","A Death in Brazil: A Book of Omissions","Peter Robb",false},
},
["04:58"]={
{"He wants to look death in the face. \003Two minutes to five\004. I took a handkerchief out of my pocket, but John Dawson ordered me to put it back. An Englishman dies with his eyes open. He wants to look death in the face.","Dawn: A Novel","Elie Wiesel",true},
},
["04:59"]={
{"The captain and his three mates appeared out of the early morning mist at \003one minute to five\004. All four of them were dressed in exactly the same clothes they had been wearing the night before, making Percy wonder if they’d come straight from the Fisherman’s Arms.","The Undiplomatic Diplomat","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"The whole place smells like death no matter what the fuck you do. Gately gets to the shelter at \0030459\004.9h and just shuts his head off as if his head had a control switch.","Infinite Jest","David Foster Wallace",false},
